    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 561\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 6543-B, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  direct  the commissioner of agriculture and markets to\n      issue a report assessing the  use  and  development  of  precision\n      agriculture  in the state with recommendations pertaining to rural\n      broadband accessibility, use and support for farmers, as  well  as\n      cost savings and higher crop yield\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This  bill would require the Department of Agriculture and Markets, in\nconsultation with the Empire State Development Corporation, to  issue  a\nreport assessing the use and development of precision agriculture in the\nState and the availability of broadband access in rural areas.\n\n  While this bill's objectives are laudable, its provisions would impose\nunbudgeted  costs  on  the  State.  Consequently,  this proposal is more\nappropriately discussed in the context  of  State  Budget  negotiations.\nTherefore, I am vetoing this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
